    <bpmn:process id="W_W1882" name="W1882. Trade Account Dormancy Detection &amp; Reactivation Campaign" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: System detects no purchase activity for 90+ days
Frequency: Monthly dormancy scan
Volume: ~200–400 dormant accounts identified/year
Owner: Account Manager
Participants: Account Manager, Marketing Team, Trade Professional
Source: workflow W1882 — Trade Account Dormancy Detection &amp; Reactivation Campaign</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1882_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1882_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1882_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1882_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1882_Lane2" name="Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1882_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1882_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1882_Lane3" name="Marketing Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1882_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1882_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1882_Start5" name="System detects no purchase activity for 90+ days">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1882_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1882_Task6" name="Monthly: system generates dormancy report: (a) accounts with no purchases in 90…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly: system generates dormancy report: (a) accounts with no purchases in 90 days: &quot;at-risk&quot;, (b) accounts with no purchases in 180 days: &quot;dormant&quot;, (c) accounts with no purchases in 365 days: &quot;churned&quot;, (d) for each account: last purchase date, trailing 12-month spend, assigned AM, store of last purchase
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Account Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1882_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1882_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1882_Task7" name="AM investigates dormancy reason: (a) call trade professional: is the business…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AM investigates dormancy reason: (a) call trade professional: is the business still active? Did they switch to a competitor? Was there a service issue? (b) common reasons: (i) project completed — between projects, (ii) competitor offered better pricing, (iii) service complaint unresolved, (iv) business slowdown or closure, (v) moved to area not served by BuildRight
Responsible (R): Account Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–30 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1882_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1882_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1882_Task8" name="Reactivation action based on reason: (a) between projects: offer project…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Reactivation action based on reason: (a) between projects: offer project pipeline support, credit limit pre-approval for upcoming project, (b) competitor pricing: review pricing competitiveness per W1881.1b; if pricing is genuinely uncompetitive, request Category Manager approval for matched or preferential pricing, (c) service issue: escalate unresolved complaint per W13.1; offer service recovery gesture (discount, priority delivery), (d) business slowdown: offer flexible terms, smaller minimum orders, (e) relocation: update primary store assignment; offer online ordering with delivery
Responsible (R): Account Manager / Marketing Team
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 30–60 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1882_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1882_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1882_Task9" name="Quarterly: Marketing Team analyzes dormancy patterns: (a) dormancy rate trend…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Quarterly: Marketing Team analyzes dormancy patterns: (a) dormancy rate trend: improving or worsening?, (b) dormancy by segment: which contractor types are most likely to go dormant?, (c) dormancy by store: are certain stores losing trade accounts at higher rates?, (d) competitive intelligence: which competitors are winning dormant accounts?, (e) reactivation success rate: % of dormant accounts successfully reactivated
Responsible (R): Marketing Team
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 day/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1882_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1882_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1882_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1882_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1882_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-370 (ensure controlled execution — Trade Account Lifecycle &amp; Relationship Management (PA-43.1).) | - operational: Account Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Account Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1882_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1882_Annotation11" targetRef="W1882_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
