    <bpmn:process id="W_W1883" name="W1883. Trade Account Churn Risk Prediction &amp; Retention Intervention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly churn risk model scoring
Frequency: Monthly model refresh; weekly review of high-risk accounts
Volume: ~5,200 active trade accounts scored monthly
Owner: FP&amp;A / Account Manager
Participants: FP&amp;A, Account Manager, VP Store Operations, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1883 — Trade Account Churn Risk Prediction &amp; Retention Intervention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1883_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1883_Lane1" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1883_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1883_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1883_Lane2" name="Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1883_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1883_Lane3" name="VP Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1883_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1883_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1883_Start5" name="Monthly churn risk model scoring">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1883_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1883_Task6" name="Monthly: FP&amp;A runs churn risk prediction model: (a) input features: (i)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monthly: FP&amp;A runs churn risk prediction model: (a) input features: (i) purchase frequency trend (declining?), (ii) spend trend (decreasing?), (iii) category breadth (narrowing?), (iv) payment behavior changes (slowing payments?), (v) return rate (increasing?), (vi) complaint frequency, (vii) engagement recency (last AM contact date), (viii) competitor activity in account&#x27;s trade area, (b) model outputs: churn risk score per account (high/medium/low), top contributing factors, predicted next-90-day spend
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1 day/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1883_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1883_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1883_Task7" name="Account Manager reviews high-risk accounts weekly: (a) accounts flagged &quot;high…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Account Manager reviews high-risk accounts weekly: (a) accounts flagged &quot;high churn risk&quot;: AM must contact within 5 business days, (b) AM investigates risk factors and develops retention plan: (i) if pricing-related: request Category Manager review for competitive pricing match, (ii) if service-related: escalate service issue with operations team, (iii) if relationship-related: schedule face-to-face meeting to rebuild rapport, (iv) if project-related: offer project support services (dedicated fulfillment, job-site delivery)
Responsible (R): Account Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 30–60 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1883_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1883_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1883_Task8" name="Monthly: VP Store Operations reviews retention metrics: (a) trade account churn…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly: VP Store Operations reviews retention metrics: (a) trade account churn rate (target: &lt; 10% annual), (b) retention intervention success rate, (c) revenue at risk: total spend of high-risk accounts, (d) model accuracy: prediction vs. actual churn (calibrate model quarterly)
Responsible (R): VP Store Operations
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1883_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1883_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1883_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1883_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1883_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-370 (ensure controlled execution — Trade Account Lifecycle &amp; Relationship Management (PA-43.1).) | - operational: FP&amp;A / Account Manager review and approval gate
Owner: FP&amp;A / Account Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
